---
layout: base.njk
---
<div class="stage">

  {# Diderot & d'Alembert, Encyclopédie (1751–1772). Ink extracted to alpha;
     tinted and parallaxed in CSS. The engravings are public domain, but the
     typecase SCAN is CC BY-SA 4.0 — the colophon credit is a licence
     condition, not decoration. Do not remove it while that plate is in use. #}
  <div class="plates" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="plate plate--forme"        data-depth="0.018"></div>
    <div class="plate plate--typecase"     data-depth="0.042"></div>
    <div class="plate plate--amphitheatre" data-depth="0.030"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="vignette" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <main class="content">

    <div class="masthead">
      <span class="masthead-name">Rafael Nepô</span>
      <span class="masthead-role">Information Architect &amp; Presentation Strategist</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="title">I turn complexity<br>into clarity.</h1>

    <p class="lede">Information architecture and presentation strategy — for
      organizations, and the teams inside them, whose message only gets one
      chance to land.</p>

    <div class="proof">
      <p class="proof-row">
        <span>C-suite &amp; senior leadership since 2012</span>
        <span>Work delivered for Gartner, NVIDIA, Blizzard &amp; others</span>
      </p>
      <p class="proof-row">
        <span>100+ conferences, workshops &amp; summits</span>
        <span>10+ countries</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    {# Tabs on wide screens, a stacked list on phones — all three titles
       stay visible either way, so the offer is never hidden. The tab roles
       are added by JS and only while tabs are actually driving; without
       scripting every panel renders in normal flow. #}
    <section class="services" aria-labelledby="services-heading">
      <h2 id="services-heading" class="visually-hidden">Areas of work</h2>

      <div class="services-bar">
        {# Separators are their own aria-hidden elements rather than
           pseudo-elements on the buttons, so "+" never leaks into a
           tab's accessible name. #}
        <div class="services-tabs">
          <button class="service-tab" id="tab-events"
                  aria-controls="panel-events">Live Events</button>
          <span class="tab-sep" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          <button class="service-tab" id="tab-strategy"
                  aria-controls="panel-strategy">Strategy &amp; Content</button>
          <span class="tab-sep" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          <button class="service-tab" id="tab-speaking"
                  aria-controls="panel-speaking">Speaking &amp; Training</button>
        </div>

        <div class="services-nav" hidden>
          <button class="services-arrow" type="button" data-step="-1"
                  aria-label="Previous area of work">&lsaquo;</button>
          <button class="services-arrow" type="button" data-step="1"
                  aria-label="Next area of work">&rsaquo;</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="service-panels">
        <div class="service-panel" id="panel-events" aria-labelledby="tab-events">
          <p>On site — presentation design and information architecture, with
            the rehearsals senior leadership needs before they shape how an
            industry thinks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-panel" id="panel-strategy" aria-labelledby="tab-strategy">
          <p>The structure of the argument — research, review and rehearsals on
            your schedule, remote or wherever the week puts you. Settled before
            anyone opens a deck.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-panel" id="panel-speaking" aria-labelledby="tab-speaking">
          <p>Keynotes, and in-company workshops that prepare your sales and
            training teams for the room — until they are able to do this
            without me.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="contact{% if site.formEndpoint %} contact--with-form{% endif %}">
      {# No standing email link: the form is the path. The address still
         reaches the visitor if the form ever fails — the error message
         below falls back to it. #}
      {% if not site.formEndpoint %}
      <div class="contact-direct">
        <a class="email" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Working%20together">{{ site.email }}</a>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if site.formEndpoint %}
      {# Plain POST by default; the script upgrades it to a background
         submit so a reply never costs the visitor the page. #}
      <form class="inquiry" action="{{ site.formEndpoint }}" method="POST"
            data-fallback="{{ site.email }}">
        <div class="field-pair">
          <label class="field">
            <span class="field-label">Name</span>
            <input type="text" name="name" maxlength="100" autocomplete="name" required>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span class="field-label">Company</span>
            <input type="text" name="company" maxlength="100" autocomplete="organization">
          </label>
        </div>

        <label class="field">
          <span class="field-label">Email</span>
          <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required>
        </label>

        <label class="field">
          <span class="field-label">What’s the occasion, and when?</span>
          <textarea name="occasion" rows="2" maxlength="1000"></textarea>
        </label>

        {# Formspree's documented honeypot: bots fill it, people never see it.
           readonly is load-bearing — password managers ignore autocomplete="off"
           and will fill this, which silently spams a real inquiry. #}
        <input class="gotcha" type="text" name="_gotcha" tabindex="-1"
               autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" readonly>

        <button class="send" type="submit">Send</button>
        <p class="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

  </main>

  <footer class="colophon">
    <p>© {{ site.founded }}–{{ site.yearShort }} {{ site.entity }} · {{ site.location }}</p>
    <p class="credit">Illustrations — plates from Diderot &amp; d’Alembert’s
      <i>Encyclopédie</i>, 1751–1772. Type case via
      <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Planche_encyclop%C3%A9die_imprimerie_3_Casse.jpg">Wikimedia
      Commons</a> / Gallica (BnF),
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p>
  </footer>

</div>
